  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThe fantastic weather will continue through the \nweekend with seasonal temperatures and low humidity. Overnight \nlows will be cool enough to wear a light jacket! Starting Monday,\nwe will see a rise in temperatures as high pressure builds back \nover the southeast. This will keep rain chances near 0% through \nTuesday and warm us back up into the upper 80s to maybe even 90 in\nNashville. Fortunately the upper air pattern appears more \nprogressive next week and a low pressure system will be swinging \nthrough during the Wednesday/Thursday timeframe. This feature will\nbring widespread rain chances back to the area to finish out the \nweek with the NBM currently giving 30-50% rain chances areawide \nWednesday afternoon through Friday. Still some model disagreement \nabout placement and strength of this low, but confidence is high \nenough to warrant PoPs in the forecast. We'll also see another drop\nin temperatures, and the spread is quite large right now given \nthe uncertainty of the low's track.",
